id: decisions/026-what-counts-as-proof
title: "A source list is not a proof"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'what-counts-as-proof'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: what-counts-as-proof
axis_gloss: "whether a claim is backed by something a machine can run, or by a cited sentence a reader must accept"
poles:
  a: executable-proof
  b: prose-proof
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 11.8
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(14) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Does a list of other .yawn files under proof.source count as proof, or is
  proof only something that can be run, observed, or replayed?

why_it_matters: >
  core/proof-and-boundary.yawn says proof can be an observed outcome, a
  completed action, an artifact, a replayed comparison, never a citation, yet 75
  of the 128 proof blocks are a list of sibling files marked seed-backed, three
  of them citing a private C:/ path, while the 15-file tests/ folder that
  carries every executable check has no node.yawn and is absent from the index.
  A bot inherits either prove-it-by-running-it or
  prove-it-by-pointing-at-another-record; a child Yawn learns which kind of
  proof block to write.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    11 judgments sit at executable-proof (1 authored) and 3 at prose-proof (0
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave counts a bot having read a document (the README audit's proof
    sources are documents it reads, J0038) as an observed outcome or as a
    citation.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      A proof block must name something that runs or was observed: a command, a
      test, a verifier, a validator_ref, a falsifier, or a dated outcome. A list of
      other .yawn files is lineage, not proof; it moves to lineage: and proof.status
      reads none until a check exists.
    cost: "75 seed-backed blocks relabelled from proof to lineage; a runnable check or none for each; tests/node.yawn written and linked from yawn.yawn."
    risk: "Most of core/ and all of automation/ read as unproven overnight, which is true but demoralizing; a bot with no check to name writes a fake one."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A new tests/proof-block-shape.test.mjs asserting every proof: block contains at least one of command, test, verifier, validator_ref, falsifier or outcome, with a frozen GRANDFATHERED map for the current seed-backed files that only shrinks; plus an assertion that tests/node.yawn exists and yawn.yawn links it."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0055"
      - "J0126"
      - "J0279"
      - "J0316"
      - "J0382"
      - "J0440"
  - name: B
    description: >
      A source list is proof at seed strength. proof.status: seed-backed means
      grounded in these records and is a valid terminal state for a record whose
      claims are conceptual.
    cost: "One sentence in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn adding cited record to proof_can_be."
    risk: "The proof_can_be list becomes false; a claim citing an unreachable C:/ file (FACT 19) stays source-backed forever; nothing distinguishes a record that was tested from one that was linked."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None beyond validating that every proof.source path resolves, which scripts/validate-hub-links.mjs does for markdown only and which is not wired into npm run validate."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0453"
      - "J0701"
      - "J1144"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Proof is executable or observed for any record with status active or v1 and
      for every automation that can act; proof.status: seed-backed remains valid for
      v0-seed and draft records and means lineage, not proof. Every proof.source
      path must resolve inside the repository. tests/ gets a node.yawn and appears
      in the index.
    cost: "Runnable checks or demotion for the 37 active or v1 files (only schemas/node.yawn names a command today); C:/ sources in references/ and automation/ replaced by in-repo copies or marked unreachable; tests/node.yawn."
    risk: "Two meanings of proof.status in one tree, told apart only by the record's status."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same test as A, scoped to status active or v1 and to automation/*.yawn, plus a path-resolution check on every proof.source entry; extend scripts/validate-hub-links.mjs to .yawn proof.source lists and wire it into npm run validate."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0055"
      - "J0279"
      - "J0316"
      - "J0382"
      - "J0440"
      - "J1144"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.7
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The authored rule (proof_can_be in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn, and J0279 in
    Dave's own models: what the child does, not what she says) is executable or
    observed; the one proof-attached judgment (J0316, dave/node.yawn with a
    validator that runs) is on the same side; 128 green assertions on 15 subjects
    (FACT 5) are where the repo actually bought proof. The prose-proof side is
    practice by volume, not by argument: the artifacts carry 75 seed-backed blocks
    and a constitutional checklist that checks only what prose can satisfy
    (J0701). A is the honest rule but would relabel most of core/ in one move; C
    applies it where status claims maturity and where a bot can act, and fixes the
    two things GROUND_TRUTH makes urgent: proof sources on a private disk (FACT
    19) and an invisible tests/ folder (FACT 4).

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "tests/ has a node.yawn and yawn.yawn links it"
    - "A test in tests/ rejects an active or v1 record, or any automation contract, whose proof block names nothing runnable or observed, passing with a shrink-only ledger"
    - "Every proof.source path resolves inside the repository, asserted by a validator in npm run validate"
    - "core/proof-and-boundary.yawn says a source list is lineage"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A record marked active carries proof.status: source-backed with a C:/Users
    path as its first source and npm test stays green;
    references/scientific-frame.yawn is the live case.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0055"
  - "J0126"
  - "J0279"
  - "J0316"
  - "J0382"
  - "J0440"
  - "J0453"
  - "J0701"
  - "J1144"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
